// Mission TT3_5, OpenTT's own map: generated.
// The Dark Cortex (tt3_5): OpenTT's own red map (a 400 m mission area), the dark fortress on the lava world.
// Layout (x east, y north; green spawns south, blue north):
// (48, 0)      the fortress: a basalt plateau (top 128 m, a terrace at 118 m on three sides,
// ramps up from the north-west and south-west), its east side a sheer 24 m cliff
// into the lava sea, basalt ramps up from the sea's shore and along the cliff's
// foot from beside the pool to the top's corners north and south of the tower; the dark tower (a black wedge splitting into two spires, 160 m
// over the plateau) at (69, 0) on the edge, its plinth down the cliff, the lava
// pouring from its foot down a scree fan into a glowing pool; one reload arch on the top before the tower;
// (152, 0)     the lava sea (104 m, level) under the tower, closed in the east by a ragged basalt
// rim (x 184, 18..30 m over the lava; the rivers leave it north-east and south-east),
// a crashed starfighter half sunk in it at (138, -14), embers rising from the lava;
// the land: dark rock terraces (6 m steps, gentle) falling from the fortress to the edges;
// the lava rivers: from the sea out to the edges, meandering in flat-bottomed channels
// (3..5 m) with crusted banks, brighter down the terrace steps: the north river round the
// fortress's north side to the west edge (its island (52, 76) between rock fords, the lava
// tube's crust bridge at (-30, 62), a branch to the north edge), the south river to the
// west edge (a rock causeway at (58, -84), the ramp jumps over its gorge at (-48, -96),
// boost pads before the lips; a branch to the south edge), shallow ones from the sea to the
// north and south edges; natural rock bridges along every river; jump pads out of the two
// big ones;
// (122, 122), (112, -128)  old lava domes with a ramp, a power-up on top;
// health in the east and west; blue's drop points green's mirrored over the x axis.
// See tt_assets::data::mission.
